                        <field name="dc_description">The dress of textile artist Waltraud Janzen “Primaballerina” is not portable. It is made of stripes of packaging foil. The stripes are intertwined into braids that are loosely sewn together. At the level of the waist, the braids jump up and form a skirt.<br/>
